{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MarkovMarginalConstant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MarkovMarginalConstant","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.margDown_ne_without_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.margDown_ne_without_step","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MarkovMarginalConstant.lean#L112-L120","doc":"**The hypothesis is load-bearing.**  Drop it and the conclusion fails: with\n`restrict` the identity and `w n = fun _ => n`, the depth-1 marginal at level\n`0` is `1`, not `w 0 = 0`.  So `margDown_eq_of_step` is not a tautology about\n`margDown`, and the step condition is doing real work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.step_satisfiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.step_satisfiable","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MarkovMarginalConstant.lean#L106-L110","doc":"The hypothesis is satisfiable: a constant tower is Markov-compatible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.marginal_functional_ne_two_valued","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.marginal_functional_ne_two_valued","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MarkovMarginalConstant.lean#L88-L99","doc":"**The exclusion, assembled.**  If the marginal is Markov-compatible and the\ntarget takes two different values, no depth reproduces the target everywhere.\n\nApplied: `F ∘ margDown` is `E₀ · S_cut`, constant in `A`; `g` is `B_AME`, which\ndiffers between `²H` and `⁷Li`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.not_forall_eq_of_const_of_two_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.not_forall_eq_of_const_of_two_values","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MarkovMarginalConstant.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**A constant cannot match a target that takes two values.**\n\nStated as a refutation of pointwise agreement rather than as `∃ c, f c ≠ g c`:\nthe negation is constructive, needing no classical step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.marginal_functional_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.marginal_functional_const","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MarkovMarginalConstant.lean#L69-L77","doc":"**Any functional of the marginal is depth-independent.**  In the application\n`F` is the von Neumann entropy of the reduced state on a fixed-width cut; the\nproof does not care what it is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.margDown_eq_of_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.margDown_eq_of_step","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MarkovMarginalConstant.lean#L55-L67","doc":"**The invariant.**  One-step compatibility forces depth-independence: the\nmarginal taken from level `n + d` is `w n`, for every depth `d`.\n\nThis is the Markov property doing the work.  The hypothesis constrains a single\nstep; the conclusion is about all of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.margDown","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.margDown","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MarkovMarginalConstant.lean#L46-L53","doc":"The marginal of the level-`(n + d)` weights, restricted down `d` steps to\nlevel `n`.  Stated for a bare `restrict`/`w` pair rather than as a field of a\nstructure, so that §\"Non-vacuity\" can instantiate it with a pair that does *not*\nsatisfy the step condition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}